KG42.register("clusters-bf1488c981660734f03f3c47",{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v142-d-CL002","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","label":"Internal pricing and iterative coordination driven by net energy declarations","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"Internal pricing and iterative coordination driven by net energy declarations","market_meaning":"Prosumers submit their net energy after scheduling, ESP aggregates supply and demand and updates internal prices, and the prices then guide prosumers in adjusting their plans; price bounds, economic balance requirements, and stopping conditions jointly constrain the formation of the final prices. The existing chains can describe the feedback process but are insufficient to form a mathematically closed solution rule.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["coordination","pricing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"The chains belong to the same sharing-area mechanism, but R001's non-scenario supply and demand aggregation has not yet been consistently connected to the scenario quantities and seller-aggregation notation in Algorithm 1. Support for economic balance is limited to 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1; numerical stopping, no further adjustments to plans, and an exact fixed point cannot be directly equated either.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Assembly is organized around the decision loop of net-quantity inputs, price updates, and feedback termination, rather than grouping by ESP nodes. R008 provides only economic balance support for price design, while fee allocation forms a separate cluster; the institutional, fairness, profit-limitation, and disclosure content in R001 is retained as governance background and is not converted into additional prerequisites for price updates.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides net-quantity declarations, aggregation in the supply and demand branches, and ESP responsibilities; its governance provisions retain their original independent meanings."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides price broadcasting, decentralized responses, the iteration limit, and the tolerance-based stopping procedure."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides price recalculation, final-price conditions, supply and demand branches, and price-design requirements."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"References only C007's conditional economic balance relationship to support price construction; not all settlement activities are included in this cluster's main rule."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-NP_i_h","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-TSP_h","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-TBP_h"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C008","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e11","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g03-E17"],"rationale":"The quoted passage connects the submission of net quantities after scheduling, supply and demand aggregation, and price updates parameterized by SDR. Only the quantity interface is marked here; R006 lacks the corresponding typed quantity objects, so this cannot be used to fabricate SDR or merge scenario and non-scenario quantities."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26"],"rationale":"The same passage describing the interaction explicitly states that ESP recalculates and broadcasts prices and that prosumers arrange their schedules according to the prices received; price formation and signal coordination therefore constitute a functional coupling."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-03"],"rationale":"Scheduling guided by prices at each step may change the net quantities, with the new results sent back to ESP; the supply and demand branches retain their respective sign conditions for net quantities. This mapping does not supply the missing local optimization constraints."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-30"],"rationale":"The algorithmic stopping procedure and the behavioral conditions for final prices jointly describe the issue of iteration termination, but satisfying the tolerance does not directly mean that all plans remain completely unchanged; the complementary formulations and their unresolved differences are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E18","v141-b-g04-e04","v141-b-g01-e13"],"rationale":"The appendix derives the internal buying price from economic balance, so the conditional balance relationship on the settlement side can support the price-design requirements; this relationship is not equivalent to complete service-fee accounts and does not automatically cover SDR > 1."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26"],"rationale":"The nodes at both locations refer to demand-quantity submission in the same iterative process. Representative selection is only for display; the submission relationship and the relationship preceding pricing are each retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26"],"rationale":"The nodes at both locations refer to supply-quantity submission in the same sharing area; unified display does not change the negative-net-quantity condition or the meanings of the edges in each chain."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM003","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g02-E-26"],"rationale":"The source explicitly identifies the same ESP as the entity receiving net quantities, updating prices, and bearing responsibility for payment balance. Node identity does not mean that these responsibilities are equivalent to one another or constitute undeclared dependencies."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM004","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26"],"rationale":"The nodes at both locations refer to the same internal-price feedback process; the final-price conditions and numerical stopping conditions remain distinct constraints."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM005","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g03-E18"],"rationale":"The nodes at all three locations represent the internal pricing function of this sharing area, used respectively for broadcasting, formation, and links to payments; this does not provide a basis for merging the price symbols or their respective constraints."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM006","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R008::V::settlement.payment"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::settlement.payment","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E18","v141-b-g04-e04"],"rationale":"The nodes at both locations are associated with the monetary payment and balance functions of the same sharing area; the price-construction statement is not merged with service fees or balance formulas."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The frozen chains do not include a complete scheduling chain representing prosumers' local optimization and its feasible region, and the update relationship from adjusted energy consumption to net quantities has not been included as a constraint in the existing chains either. Therefore, the decision step from price feedback to new declared quantities is not yet mathematically closed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-NP_i_h","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-12","v141-b-g02-E-18","v141-b-g02-E-22","v141-b-g02-E-26"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P1","v141-b-g03-P01"],"required_work":"Formal chains and object references for scheduling objectives, feasible regions, and net-quantity updates are to be supplied upstream, and the relevant unapproved proposals are to be processed manually; D does not substitute participation nodes or declaration nodes for load scheduling actions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G004","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R006's pricing content remains a frozen procedural statement, lacking an SDR definition, a complete buying-price construction, and typed input references; R008-C007 can provide only partial economic balance support. The definition of SDR and the treatment of prices when TBP^h is zero are also unspecified, and this case cannot automatically be assigned to SDR > 1.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-TBP_h","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C008","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C009","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g03-P02"],"required_work":"Complete the mathematical pricing objects, references, and domains in an explicitly specified subsequent revision of C, and check the zero-demand case; v141-b-g03-P02 remains pending, and D is not to insert an SDR node or repair the C2 candidate that was not adopted."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G005","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"Stopping based on a price-difference tolerance, all prosumers ceasing to adjust their plans, and an exact fixed point are conditions at different levels. R002 lacks the corresponding typed price and tolerance objects; the supplied discussion of fixed-point existence also cannot prove that Algorithm 1 converges in all scenarios.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-30","v141-b-g03-E32"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Specify upstream the objects, norm, and scope of applicability of the stopping metric, and retain the distinction between numerical stopping and a behavioral fixed point; do not eliminate the differences through a same_expression mapping or generalize case-specific convergence results into a guarantee."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G006","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The current B text of Algorithm 1 sums negative net quantities without the minus sign used in R001's seller aggregation, conflicting with the nonnegative TSP convention; the algorithm also uses scenario indices, whereas the existing aggregation objects have no scenario indices. It cannot be determined whether the differences originate in transcription or in the source, and day-ahead and hour-ahead quantities cannot be directly unified either.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-TSP_h","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C009","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-24","v141-b-g02-E-25","v141-b-g02-E-28"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually compare Algorithm 1 with the supply and demand definitions to check the symbols, and specify upstream the respective interfaces for day-ahead, hour-ahead, and scenario quantities; both the current C aggregation expressions and the B text remain unchanged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G007","category":"ontology_extension","description":"R001 also retains governance content such as institutional arrangements, an impartiality objective, profit limits, and a fairness index that may be disclosed daily. This content cannot serve as stopping conditions for pricing; calculation of the fairness index has not yet entered the frozen chains, v141-b-g04-p1 remains unapproved, and the fairness index K cannot be unified with the iteration limit K on the basis of their shared symbol.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-E-39","v141-b-g04-e31","v141-b-g04-e34"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g04-p1"],"required_work":"If fairness-calculation and disclosure rules need to be assembled independently, their objects and chain boundaries should be specified upstream, and the proposal should be processed manually; currently, only the governance background and permission to disclose are retained, without adding numerical profit caps or new dependencies."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G008","category":"unverified_source","description":"All connections and node-display mappings in this cluster use unaudited B candidate evidence permitted by the experiment; the symbols, algorithm, and formula transcriptions have not received independent source verification.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e11","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the sources and all assembly relationships item by item, prioritizing aggregation symbols, scenario scope, and pricing formulas; candidate eligibility in this round does not indicate that B or the downstream scientific content has passed independent review."}]},"rule_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R001","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R002","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-20e312b579d3a493","COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","COMP-c6917f781ea3f39e","COMP-dddaa2edb4acd670","KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","KG31-a9bd9e360b96ff06","KG31-e3df7b859b17cba0"]});
